From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:33:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] sync: transport anchored UTXO snapshots and reverse proofs

Add bijective reverse block peeling (GETBLOCKUNDO / BLOCKUNDO) to verify
historical blocks backwards from the SnapSync pivot to genesis.

Original-Commit: a16ac06fc43b52ac5632553554a94afba2e222be
Original-Patch: ecash/017
Split-Concern: whole

Historical compilation prerequisites are tracked separately in daemon/patch-audit;
this provenance-preserving split does not imply standalone build validation.

Candidate-purpose: Complete the peer transport for the preceding state engine:
capability negotiation, bounded shard swarm, authenticated-root and undo exchange,
peer lifecycle and the historical Byzantine-peer regression fixture. The engine
owns legacy conversion, atomic installation and consensus validation. Late
catch-up definitions are folded here rather than left as a broken forward API.

Candidate-Repair: Complete shared transport with the required processor include, start/status RPCs and CLI conversions; wire ABC-accepted requested historical bodies to queued undo replay, add idle-peer request deadlines through SendMessages, and preserve all reverse validation assertions with pruned-body/corrupt-body/timeout regressions plus real two-node transfer/restart/opt-out coverage. Native 10 cases/2222 assertions and functional pass; omitted production hooks fail four unchanged assertions. Generic RPC ownership moves from future V2/040; V2-specific controls remain there.

Candidate-Repair: Clean 23 exposed eight existing Avalanche processor-replacement fixtures dereferencing a freed processor from redundant peer initialization. Remove that initialization write: unknown peers already default to no state-anchor support and Processor::FinalizeNode clears negotiated support. Wire actual swarm RemovePeer at PeerManager::FinalizeNode to remove raw node pointers and trigger failover; add disconnected-peer ineligibility assertions. All 123 Avalanche cases and 10 handler cases pass manually; clean replay required.
